IMPORT prelude

-- g1-interpretation.l4: the fork points of Articles 1 and 2 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, in the R4 shape of the brief.
-- One fork point is one enumeration with one constructor per reading; all of them are fields of ONE record, `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`,
-- each field TYPICALLY the reading taken. Every public decision of g1-art1-defined-terms, g1-art2-entity and g1-art2-governor-misconduct that depends on a
-- fork takes this record as an ordinary GIVEN and delegates by CONSIDER to one private implementation per reading, so each reading is a callable function.
-- The register of forks (provision, readings, the text that licenses each, the reading taken and why, the discriminating case) is in FRAGMENT-G1.md.
-- Nothing here depends on the Law's wording beyond the names of the readings; the readings are explained where the fork is used.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation: the forks of Articles 1 and 2`

-- F1.1 (Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) against the inserted 2(1)(ba)): does "(a) to (h)" reach (ba)?
@ref Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) (fork F1.1)
DECLARE `How the ranges (a) to (h) in Article 2 treat sub-paragraph (ba)` IS ONE OF
    `the ranges follow the letters of the amended list, so (ba) is inside (a) to (h)`
    `the ranges are read as of the enactment of the Law, so (ba) is outside (a) to (h)`

-- F1.2 (Article 2(10)(b)): do the words "in relation to a registered charity ..." govern every limb (i) to (vi)?
@ref Article 2(10)(b) (fork F1.2)
DECLARE `What the words in relation to a registered charity govern in Article 2(10)(b)` IS ONE OF
    `every limb (i) to (vi) needs the offence to be in relation to a charity or an equivalent entity`
    `only limb (i) is tied to the charity, and limbs (ii) to (vi) apply to an offence by any person`

-- F1.3 (Article 2(5)(e) against 2(1)(g) and (h)): what is the constitutional Law of a body incorporated "under, but not by" an enactment?
@ref Article 2(5)(e), 2(1)(g), 2(1)(h) (fork F1.3)
DECLARE `The constitutional Law of a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)`
    `the enactment under which the body is incorporated`

-- F1.4 (Article 2(4) to 2(7) and 8(3)(a)(i)): the definitions are lists of cases ("in the case of a trust ...", "in the case of a company ..."),
-- and Article 8(3)(a)(i) shows that one entity can be in the case of both a trust (a) and a company (f). Which cases apply to such an entity?
@ref Article 2(4) to 2(7), 8(3)(a)(i) (fork F1.4)
DECLARE `How the cases of Article 2(4) to (7) combine for a body in more than one kind` IS ONE OF
    `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies`
    `only the first case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies, in the order the paragraph lists them`

-- F1.5 (Article 1 "publish", used by 2(8)(b)(i)): is information published when the publisher so thinks, or when the manner is in fact likely to reach the audience?
@ref Article 1, definition of “publish” (fork F1.5)
DECLARE `What makes information published under Article 1` IS ONE OF
    `the opinion of the person publishing`
    `the likelihood of the manner, judged objectively`

-- F1.6 (Article 2(1)(e)): "in relation to Jersey" follows sub-paragraph (iii) only, or the whole list?
@ref Article 2(1)(e) (fork F1.6)
DECLARE `What the words in relation to Jersey qualify in Article 2(1)(e)` IS ONE OF
    `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)`
    `each of sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii)`

-- F1.7 (Article 1 "registered charity ... for the time being", used by 2(10)(a) and (b)): the standing of the charity is read at the time of the conduct, or when the question is asked?
@ref Article 1, definition of “registered charity”; Article 2(10) (fork F1.7)
DECLARE `When the standing of a registered charity is read for Article 2(10)` IS ONE OF
    `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred`
    `when the question under Article 2(10) is asked`

-- F1.8 (Article 2(1)(g) against 2(1)(c) and (d)): (g) names every enactment but the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991, so read as written it also takes in a foundation
-- (incorporated under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009) and an incorporated 1862 association. Does (g) overlap them?
@ref Article 2(1)(g) (fork F1.8)
DECLARE `Whether sub-paragraph (g) overlaps sub-paragraphs (c), (d) and (f)` IS ONE OF
    `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)`
    `(g) is the residue, so a body within (c), (d) or (f) is not also within (g)`

@ref Articles 1 and 2 (the record of the forks F1.1 to F1.8)
DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` HAS
    -- F1.1
    `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)` IS A `How the ranges (a) to (h) in Article 2 treat sub-paragraph (ba)`
        TYPICALLY `the ranges follow the letters of the amended list, so (ba) is inside (a) to (h)`
    -- F1.2
    `limbs of Article 2(10)(b)` IS A `What the words in relation to a registered charity govern in Article 2(10)(b)`
        TYPICALLY `every limb (i) to (vi) needs the offence to be in relation to a charity or an equivalent entity`
    -- F1.3
    `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` IS A `The constitutional Law of a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`
        TYPICALLY `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)`
    -- F1.4
    `cases for a body in more than one kind` IS A `How the cases of Article 2(4) to (7) combine for a body in more than one kind`
        TYPICALLY `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies`
    -- F1.5
    `meaning of published` IS A `What makes information published under Article 1`
        TYPICALLY `the opinion of the person publishing`
    -- F1.6
    `reach of in relation to Jersey` IS A `What the words in relation to Jersey qualify in Article 2(1)(e)`
        TYPICALLY `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)`
    -- F1.7
    `time of the standing of a charity` IS A `When the standing of a registered charity is read for Article 2(10)`
        TYPICALLY `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred`
    -- F1.8
    `overlap of sub-paragraph (g)` IS A `Whether sub-paragraph (g) overlaps sub-paragraphs (c), (d) and (f)`
        TYPICALLY `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)`

§§ `The readings, as values`

-- The reading taken at every fork, and for each fork the other reading with every other fork left at the reading taken.
@ref Articles 1 and 2 (the reading taken at every fork)
`the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` WITH
        `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `the ranges follow the letters of the amended list, so (ba) is inside (a) to (h)`
        `limbs of Article 2(10)(b)` IS `every limb (i) to (vi) needs the offence to be in relation to a charity or an equivalent entity`
        `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` IS `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)`
        `cases for a body in more than one kind` IS `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies`
        `meaning of published` IS `the opinion of the person publishing`
        `reach of in relation to Jersey` IS `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)`
        `time of the standing of a charity` IS `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred`
        `overlap of sub-paragraph (g)` IS `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)`

@ref Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) (fork F1.1)
`the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` WITH
        `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `the ranges are read as of the enactment of the Law, so (ba) is outside (a) to (h)`
        `limbs of Article 2(10)(b)` IS `every limb (i) to (vi) needs the offence to be in relation to a charity or an equivalent entity`
        `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` IS `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)`
        `cases for a body in more than one kind` IS `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies`
        `meaning of published` IS `the opinion of the person publishing`
        `reach of in relation to Jersey` IS `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)`
        `time of the standing of a charity` IS `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred`
        `overlap of sub-paragraph (g)` IS `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)`

@ref Article 2(10)(b) (fork F1.2)
`the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` MEANS
